      "source": "import re\n\ndef slugify(title):\n    if not title:\n        return \"\"\n    title = title.lower()\n    title = re.sub(r'[^a-zA-Z0-9\\-]+', '-', title)\n    slug = re.sub(r'-+', '-', title)\n    return slug.strip('-')\n",
      "rationale": "The function first handles the empty string case. Then, it converts the title to lowercase and replaces all sequences of non-alphanumeric characters with hyphens. Finally, it removes consecutive hyphens and strips leading/trailing hyphens to produce the URL slug.",
